October 1929

{
Mention of Afghan Sahib Laghari
}

My two brothers and I were bound together in the bonds of brotherhood with pieces of our hearts. The blood of Pashtunwali surged through the veins of every member of my family. When the sound of the drum of freedom for this land, in the name of the Afghan Voice, spread through the atmosphere of the Kabul airport, a passion was ignited in the heart of my elder brother, Afghan Sahib Laghari, which changed the course of his life. He started a movement for the freedom of the oppressed Pashtun nation that sent tremors through the heart of colonialism. According to him, the struggle for freedom is not only a political necessity but also a part of our faith. He would always say: "If we want to taste the flavor of independence, we must buy it with the offering of blood." He spent most of his life in prisons, exile, and struggle, but his resolve was as firm as a mountain. In his struggle, there was a powerful voice for the unity of Pashtuns and against foreign interference. The story of his life is not just the story of one person, but the story of the epic and honor of an entire nation. He was not only a political leader but also a great symbol of the awakening of the Pashtun nation. Every word of his gave a new spirit to the Pashtun nation, and in his memory, the flames of independence still burn in the heart of every Pashtun today.

As we seek any kind of new information regarding a specific event in this love, it has an impact not only on their lives but also on historical changes. In his life, the signs of the struggle for the rights of the people of Pashtunkhwa are very clear. He gave a new color and form to the anti-colonial struggle. Upon hearing his speeches, the passions of independence were ignited in the hearts of the Pashtuns. He would say that we will not rest until our land is freed from the clutches of foreigners. There were many bitter experiences in his life, but his patience and perseverance were an example for the Pashtuns. He laid such a foundation for the purpose of the unity of the Pashtun nation that, thanks to it today, the hope for the revival of independence is alive in the hearts of the people of Pashtunkhwa.
